# xxri OS Lite dock - wbar's own configuration triple ONLY (Phase 10.2,
# repointed for the pin/unpin dock).
#
# The PINNED launchers themselves are no longer listed here.  They live in
# /usr/local/share/xxri-launcher/pinned.list (one .desktop id per line, dock
# order, max 8) and are turned into the actual triples below by
# `xxri-dock-pin boot|regen`, which looks up each id's icon/name/command
# straight from its .desktop file - the same file the All Apps drawer reads,
# so the dock and the drawer can never show two different icons for the same
# app.  This file supplies only the very first i:/t:/c: triple (wbar's own
# options line, not a launcher) - xxri-dock-pin's write_dock() pulls exactly
# that first triple out of this file and appends the generated ones after it.
#
# NOTE: comments here must never contain the dock-parser tokens ("i: ", "t: ",
# "c: " at the start of a line), because write_dock()'s own extraction is a
# plain line-pattern match too.
#
# The icon zoom is deliberately tiny (-zoomf 1.06).  At the old 1.25 every icon
# slid sideways as the pointer approached, which moved the click target out
# from under the pointer and pulled the running indicators off their icons.
# Turning zoom off altogether is NOT an option: with -zoomf 1.0 -nanim 0 wbar
# stops resolving clicks to an icon at all and the whole dock goes dead, which
# is why this is a small number rather than none.
i: /usr/local/share/xxri-theme/wbar-bg.png
t: /usr/local/lib/X11/fonts/TTF/luxisr/9
c: wbar -bpress -nofont -pos bottom -offset 15 -isize 40 -idist 7 -zoomf 1.06 -nanim 3 -jumpf 0.0
